      "writtenOn": "2022-03-16T16:08:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e \u003e I could give it a try and see how the maintainers like it.\n\u003e \n\u003e This is in our repos tho?\n\nThe problem is that the original option is defined in a file sourced from https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/main/arch/Kconfig#L12, so that\u0027s the one I would have to change to a wildcard and add \"if ARCH_*\" to all architecture Kconfig files (and there few other sets of those under soc/). If I just source all arch here and just put the override in an \"if\", the parser would try to parse and complain for missing type anyway.\n\n\u003e \n\u003e \u003e Though I don\u0027t mind separate per-arch override files either, does not look to bad with the optional source.\n\u003e \n\u003e The issue is that it becomes difficult to grok the Kconfig outside of the Zephyr build system, which seems useful to do.\n\u003e \n\u003e We\u0027re blocked on doing so by upstream zephyr not doing that, but I think we should work with them to fix that.",
